# API (Vercel)

- Vercel owns identity, authorization, and metadata. It never touches file bytes.
- Every HTTP body is Zod-parsed from `@meownow/protocol`.
- CSRF: `SameSite=Lax` plus an explicit `Origin` check on every mutating route. Both, not either.
- Sessions: opaque 256-bit token in `httpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`. Not a JWT. Instant revocation.
- Uploads: mint a 60s EdDSA capability token scoped to one server-generated R2 key and a byte cap. Client never chooses the R2 key.
- UI gating is not enforcement. Test the denial path for every permission.

```ts
// BAD
if (session.user.canUpload) await putToR2(req.body);

// GOOD
// POST /api/uploads/intent checks can_upload and quota, then mints a token.
// The Worker is the only process that writes to R2, after verifying that token.
```
